$ whaleshark     # as the person
  init      set this project up, check what it needs, and offer the rules for the lead agent  (not built yet)
  doctor    one line per check, each with its fix  (not built yet)
  guide     the guide that matches this version  (not built yet)
  trust     show what the project's settings would run or reach, and approve it  (not built yet)
  help      this list, or one command in full
  version   version, build, and the engine's version seen
  dash      the page's server for this login, and its door for phones  (not built yet)
  connect   from your own computer: keep one connection to the server for the page and the terminals  (not built yet)
  server    for the administrator, with sudo, on the server: set it up, add people, upgrade  (not built yet)
  ui        open or close the fleet pane and the action pane in the lead agent's tab  (not built yet)
  open      the window: your tabs and panes in this terminal; closing it stops nothing  (not built yet)
  engine    the keeper that holds every pane's terminal for this login: run it, stop it, see it  (not built yet)
  set       your own settings: theme, dnd, mute, nudge.sound, nudge.popup, nudge.phone, actions, fleet.width  (not built yet)
  hook      run by an agent's own harness, never typed  (not built yet)
  run       start, list, show, switch, close or delete a run, or bind it to this pane  (not built yet)
  task      add a task with its brief and its check, change it, cancel it or reset it  (not built yet)
  start     start a worker for each task, each in a tab named after it; run it in the background  (not built yet)
  wait      block until something happens, then hand out the oldest batch of events  (not built yet)
  answer    answer a question or an item; --undo reopens one whose answer nothing has used yet  (not built yet)
  escalate  mark a worker's question as one for the human  (not built yet)
  need      put an item in front of the person, or withdraw one  (not built yet)
  tell      send a worker a message; tell lead is the person's note to the lead agent  (not built yet)
  accept    run the task's check and, when it passes, keep the work; several tasks at once from phase 2  (not built yet)
  reject    send a result back to the same agent, or to ready if it is proven gone  (not built yet)
  stop      stop a task's attempt and close its tab  (not built yet)
  close     close the tabs of attempts that have ended  (not built yet)
  pause     Stop all: every agent stops at its next step and nothing new starts  (not built yet)
  resume    end the pause and tell each paused agent to carry on  (not built yet)
  team      saved teams: a set of tasks kept as a file and added to a run in one step  (not built yet)
  report    say that the task is finished, or that it could not be  (not built yet)
  progress  note how far the work is  (not built yet)
  ask       ask a question and wait for the answer  (not built yet)
  mail      read the messages from the orchestrator  (not built yet)
  status    the team, with what waits for the person on top  (not built yet)
  graph     the plan: tasks in the order they depend on each other  (not built yet)
  log       the messages both ways, newest last  (not built yet)
  show      one task in full, with what to do next on top  (not built yet)
  jump      go to a task's tab, or back to the lead agent's  (not built yet)
  catchup   what happened while you were away  (not built yet)
  overlap   files touched by more than one task, and pairs that would conflict  (not built yet)
  sync      send a worker the brief for bringing its copy up to date  (not built yet)
  land      check the collected work, then open one pull request or merge it; the lead agent only if the project allows  (not built yet)
exit 0

$ whaleshark help start    # as the person
whaleshark start <task>... | --ready [--retry] [--resume] [--agent KIND] [--model M] [--allow-overlap]
  start a worker for each task, each in a tab named after it; run it in the background

For:      the lead agent, the person
Flags:    --ready
          --retry
          --resume  (phase 2)
          --agent KIND
          --model M
          --allow-overlap
Always:   --json, --run ID, --root DIR, --help, --human, --file PATH
Exits:    0 done, 1 failed, 3 environment unusable, 5 refused
Example:  whaleshark start T3

Not built yet: it comes with phase 1.
exit 0

$ whaleshark help run    # as the person
whaleshark run new "<objective>" [--base REF] [--limit N] [--park]
whaleshark run list
whaleshark run show
whaleshark run use <id>
whaleshark run close [--abandon]
whaleshark run rm <id>
whaleshark run takeover
  start, list, show, switch, close or delete a run, or bind it to this pane

For:      the lead agent, the person
          run new: the lead agent, the person, a tab not bound to a run
          run takeover: the lead agent, the person, a tab not bound to a run
          run use: the lead agent, the person, a tab not bound to a run
          run list: the lead agent, the person, a tab not bound to a run
          run show: the lead agent, the person, a tab not bound to a run
Flags:    --base REF
          --limit N
          --park
          --abandon
Always:   --json, --run ID, --root DIR, --help, --human, --file PATH
Exits:    0 done, 4 not found, 5 refused
Example:  whaleshark run close

Not built yet: it comes with phase 1.
exit 0

